  "body": "## Summary\n\nSplit the viewport along its existing domain seams. This is a code-only move.\nThere is no intended rendering, public API, shader or safety behavior change.\n\n- Keep `viewport` as the public facade and the owner of private GPU resources.\n- Move construction, uploads, rendering, readback and WGSL to private modules.\n- Split the orbit camera from its private projection implementation.\n- Keep all method bodies and shader composition unchanged.\n- Keep the existing pipeline, wide-line and test files unchanged.\n\nEffort: medium. The maintainer classified this as no new behavior:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3052#issuecomment-7047618632\n\nWriter record:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3052#issuecomment-7221431845\n\nExact starting base: `NeoTech/Camcraft main 9fb406cd646c55ce12058dfd2930f509892240f1`.\nThis branch starts directly from upstream. It does not change the fork's main branch.\nHead: `c65b9dabf82b6af8dbd2dc59718a6fc4452abac6`.\n\n## Readings\n\nLine counts include comments and blank lines.\n\n| Viewport source file | Before | After |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `viewport.rs` | 1313 | 166 |\n| `viewport/camera.rs` | — | 251 |\n| `viewport/camera/projection.rs` | — | 228 |\n| `viewport/init.rs` | — | 156 |\n| `viewport/upload.rs` | — | 201 |\n| `viewport/render.rs` | — | 155 |\n| `viewport/readback.rs` | — | 76 |\n| `viewport/shader.rs` | — | 129 |\n| `viewport/pipes.rs` | 235 | 235 |\n| `viewport/wide.rs` | 188 | 188 |\n| `viewport/wide_tests.rs` | 61 | 61 |\n\nAll viewport source files are below 400 lines.\nThe UI source inventory keeps 1,956 test functions and 9,187 assertion macros.\nEvery existing test file and viewport child remains byte-identical.\nAn exact-block comparison accounts for every nonstructural line from the original file.\nOnly private module declarations, imports, implementation wrappers and shader visibility are added.\n`Camera` and `ProjectionMode` remain available through their existing public paths.\n\n## Verification\n\nLinux, Rust 1.100.0, three build/test jobs, `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\nGPU checks use `CAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1`, with llvmpipe/Vulkan.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base 9fb406cd646c55ce12058dfd2930f509892240f1`: PASS.\n  - UI lib: 1,760 passed, 8 existing ignored tests.\n  - `catalog_render`: 2 passed, 1 existing ignored capture.\n  - `gpu_render`: 19 passed, 1 existing ignored release snapshot.\n  - Includes the camera, orthographic picking, draw partition and wide-line unit tests.\n  - Includes rendered display modes, stock, fills, shadows, occlusion, wide lines and MSAA.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: PASS.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'`: PASS.\n  All 11 light twins run in the five named test steps. Each step compiles its own target.\n  Only the redundant all-target release prebuild is omitted.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test trace_composite -- --nocapture --test-threads=1`: PASS, 5 tests.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test theme_files -- --test-threads=3`: PASS, 30 tests, including the source color-literal guard.\n- `git diff --check 9fb406cd646c55ce12058dfd2930f509892240f1 HEAD`: PASS.\n\n### Actual output equivalence\n\nBefore editing, the unchanged catalog capture ran on the exact starting base.\nIt ran again after the split, using the same adapter and `2d/first-part` project:\n\n```sh\nCAMCRAFT_REQUIRE_GPU=1 CAMCRAFT_CATALOG_CASE=2d/first-part \\\nCAMCRAFT_CATALOG_SCREENSHOTS_OUT=<separate-before-or-after-directory> \\\ncargo test -p camcraft-ui --test catalog_render \\\n  render_all_catalog_screenshots -- --ignored --exact --nocapture --test-threads=1\n```\n\nThe four 1200×760 PNGs are byte-identical, including the blank selection and each operation.\nThis means zero different decoded pixels in those four scenes.\nTheir SHA-256 values match before and after:\n\n| Capture | SHA-256 |\n|---|---|\n| `0-blank.png` | `775c1b45bac37d828d9b010491fb21f6cdf320461383833c87cae81666c60273` |\n| `1-Face1.png` | `2fb239a5284c65460d7bb1f0b3257efdcfef2e972065d566d2e97c3f6e78ad4f` |\n| `2-2D-Pocket1.png` | `3a5aaf82750a8379471791516e10380c5cf5ecf4947e47b6147f931c79aff383` |\n| `3-Drill1.png` | `d717ea1d9d6080b84dd38169e2ee17e4d833d60595e950723a80d93deca34b37` |\n\n#### Before/after viewport images\n\nBefore source: `9fb406cd646c55ce12058dfd2930f509892240f1`.\nAfter source: `c65b9dabf82b6af8dbd2dc59718a6fc4452abac6`.\nThe saved captures use the same `2d/first-part` project, 1200×760 viewport and llvmpipe (LLVM 21.1.8)/Vulkan adapter.\nThese are unmodified viewport-only renders from the existing catalog harness, not full-window or dialog captures.\nEach before/after pair is byte-identical. A separate rerender on the after source also matches all four captures.\nOnly the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch holds these images. No image enters this PR's source branch.\n\nImages commit: [`e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9`](https://github.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/tree/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052).\n\n| Scene | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| No operation selected | ![Before — No operation selected](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/before/0-blank.png) | ![After — No operation selected](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/after/0-blank.png) |\n| Face1 | ![Before — Face1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/before/1-Face1.png) | ![After — Face1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/after/1-Face1.png) |\n| 2D-Pocket1 | ![Before — 2D-Pocket1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/before/2-2D-Pocket1.png) | ![After — 2D-Pocket1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/after/2-2D-Pocket1.png) |\n| Drill1 | ![Before — Drill1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/before/3-Drill1.png) | ![After — Drill1](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e749b883b83773305fe05fe661a383f177f2eee9/3052/after/3-Drill1.png) |\nNo golden is refreshed. The captures are test evidence, not replacement goldens.\n\n## Limits and decisions\n\nThe byte comparison covers one catalog project, not every possible scene or GPU.\nOther rendering modes are exercised by the existing GPU regression assertions.\nNo new behavior test is added for an unchanged implementation.\nThe pinning evidence is the exact source-block comparison, preserved tests and actual render comparison.\nFull workspace, batch, heavy, release-snapshot and example-generation gates are not run.\nNo post, toolpath generator, dependency, process file or physical machine is changed.\nThese are software checks, not physical-machine safety acceptance.\n\nSee `docs/decisions/3052-split-viewport.md` for the seam choices and rejected alternatives.\n\nChangelog: none (internal code-only move; no behavior change).\n\nFixes #3052\n",
